            "verdict": "warn",
            "summary": "One high finding: note paths from the search box reach the file system unchecked.",
            "counts": {
              "critical": 0,
              "high": 1,
              "medium": 1,
              "low": 0
            },
            "markdown": "## Summary\n\norbit-notes is in good shape: no secrets in the repo, dependencies are current, and the server only listens on 127.0.0.1. One path issue needs a fix before release.\n\n## Findings\n\n### High \u00b7 Path traversal when opening a note\n\n`src/search.ts:14` joins the note path from the URL with the notes folder without checking the result stays inside it. `../../.ssh/config` would be read. Resolve the path and refuse anything outside the folder.\n\n### Medium \u00b7 Search query is not length-limited\n\n`src/search.ts:9` passes the raw query to FTS5. A very long query blocks the event loop. Cap it at 200 characters.\n\n## What to do next\n\n1. Add a path guard in `openNote()` with a test for `../`.\n2. Cap the query length.\n3. Run the scan again."
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  },
